- helm
- net
- pass
- mesa_foot
- desk

' The actors that give the foot at /io/mesa a socket and a clock, and the
' loop that runs its rules (mesa_foot). Nothing here decides anything: it
' carries bytes, tells the rules what arrived, and does what they ask.
'
' The foot's own record, /<self>/io/mesa, says where it listens and where
' its two files are: `port`, `ring` (the world's signing seed, 32 bytes) and
' `mark` (its rift and the highest epoch it has announced). Both files are
' outside the world on purpose: the seed is never a record, and the mark
' must survive a restore of the world to show that one happened. Each
' peer's card, /<self>/io/mesa/<peer>, says its `key`, and its `host` and
' `port`.
'
' Bytes cross as short connections. One connection is: the sender's number
' in 16 bytes, then each packet behind its length in 4. Who a connection
' claims to be from is not believed for anything but where an answer goes:
' an answer is sent to the address this world holds for that peer, never
' back along the connection, and every page is signed.
'
' Two more files are the foot's, made when its desk first needs them:
' `custody` and `maker` (desk.foil). What a door is handed for the foot, an
' invitation's secret, is a file in io/mesa/in named by a number; what the
' foot leaves for the door, the secret of an invitation it minted, is a
' file in io/mesa/out. The desk answers while the foot is silent too: a
' world prepared under another's key becomes its own by a claim.
'
' The foot stops when its record is removed or holds `stop`: it stops its
' clock and its acceptors, closes its listening socket and ends.
'
' A world whose own card holds an identity log signs with the key the log
' states. When the log moves to a new key the foot reads its ring again;
' while the ring's key and the log's disagree it says and hears nothing.
+ mesa_wire
  + heard
    ' The packets of one connection and the number their sender gave.
    : from=nat packets=row[nat]
  + tick
    : now=nat
  + task
    & feet/task/ack
      feet/task/fact
      feet/task/admitted
      feet/task/committed
      feet/task/state
      mesa_wire/heard
      mesa_wire/tick
  + frames
    ' One connection's bytes.
    \ me=nat packets=row[nat]
    ^ nat
    % at=nat 0
      raw=nat (mod me (bex 128))
      size=nat 16
    ^ nat
    ? (ge at packets.len) (add raw (bex (mul 8 size)))
    = packet packets.at(at)
      len (dec (wid packet))
      body (mod packet (bex (mul 8 len)))
      headed (add raw (lsh len (mul 8 size)))
    | _ at.inc (add headed (lsh body (mul 8 (add size 4)))) (add size (add 4 len))
  + unframe
    ' The packets in one connection's bytes; none when they are not frames.
    \ bytes=nat
    ^ maybe[mesa_wire/heard]
    = none=maybe[mesa_wire/heard] .none
      empty=row[nat] []
      size (dec (wid bytes))
    ? (lt size 16) none
    = from (loadvar 0 16 bytes)
    % at=nat 16
      out=row[nat] empty
    ^ maybe[mesa_wire/heard]
    ? (eq at size) (./some (mesa_wire/heard from out))
    ? (gt (add at 4) size) none
    = len (loadvar at 4 bytes)
      end (add (add at 4) len)
    ? (gt end size) none
    | _ end out.snoc((add (loadvar (add at 4) len bytes) (bex (mul 8 len))))
  + acceptor
    ' Waits on the shared listening socket, reads one connection to its
    ' end, tells the foot what it carried, and waits again when the foot
    ' says to go on. The foot's answer is what stops it: a foot that is
    ' stopping connects to itself to wake each acceptor and answers no.
    \ fd=nat self=nat
    ^ nat
    = ;[hello caps] (Recv[nat] 0)
      foot caps.at(0)
      nothing=row[nat] []
      none=maybe[mesa_wire/heard] .none
    % ignored=nat 0
    = ;connection (Accept fd)
      ;bytes (ReadAll connection mesa_foot/most_read)
      got=maybe[mesa_wire/heard] (? (eq 0 bytes) none (mesa_wire/unframe bytes))
      carried got.fall((mesa_wire/heard 0 nothing))
    ; (CloseFd connection)
    ; (SendCaps foot carried [0])
    = ;[go more] (Recv[nat] 0)
    ; (helm/supervisor/close_caps more)
    ? !(go) 0
    | _ 0
  + sender
    ' Carries what the foot sends to one peer: each batch is one
    ' connection. A peer that cannot be reached loses the batch; the
    ' engine asks again and hints repeat, so nothing is queued.
    \ host=str port=nat me=nat self=nat
    ^ nat
    % ignored=nat 0
    = ;[batch caps] (Recv[row[nat]] 0)
    ; (helm/supervisor/close_caps caps)
    ; (SendTo 0 host port (mesa_wire/frames me batch))
    | _ 0
  + ticker
    ' Tells the foot the time each second, for as long as the foot says
    ' to go on.
    \ self=nat
    ^ nat
    = ;[hello caps] (Recv[nat] 0)
      foot caps.at(0)
    % ignored=nat 0
    ; (Sleep 1)
    ; (SendCaps foot (mesa_wire/tick (div (Now 0) 1000000)) [0])
    = ;[go more] (Recv[nat] 0)
    ; (helm/supervisor/close_caps more)
    ? !(go) 0
    | _ 0
  + route
    ' A peer as the foot's binding gives it, with where it is reached.
    : peer=mesa_foot/peer host=str port=nat
  + routes
    ' The peers a binding names: each child that holds a key and an address.
    \ binding=axal[saga]
    ^ row[mesa_wire/route]
    = none=row[mesa_wire/route] []
    | binding.kid_tap.fold none
      \ out=row[mesa_wire/route] [key tree]
      ^ row[mesa_wire/route]
      ?> (./some version) tree.fil out
      = card (unpin version.myth)
        held card.nat_at(['key] 0)
        port card.nat_at(['port] 0)
      ? (eq 0 held) out
      ? (eq 0 port) out
      | out.snoc((mesa_wire/route (mesa_foot/peer key (quip_val key) held) card.txt_at(['host]) port))
  + own
    \ binding=axal[saga]
    ^ myth
    ?> (./some version) binding.fil myth/new
    | unpin version.myth
  + link
    ' A sender for one peer, and the handle the foot reaches it by.
    : id=nat host=str port=nat handle=nat
  + wire
    ' Senders for the peers a binding names, keeping those whose address
    ' did not change.
    \ me=nat wanted=row[mesa_wire/route] had=row[mesa_wire/link]
    ^ row[mesa_wire/link]
    = none=row[mesa_wire/link] []
      ;kept
        | had.fold none
          \ ;out=row[mesa_wire/link] item=mesa_wire/link
          ^ row[mesa_wire/link]
          ? (wanted.any((\ want=mesa_wire/route (and (eq want.peer.id item.id) (and (equal[str] want.host item.host) (eq want.port item.port)))))) out.snoc(item)
          ; (CloseHandle item.handle)
          out
    | wanted.fold kept
      \ ;out=row[mesa_wire/link] want=mesa_wire/route
      ^ row[mesa_wire/link]
      ? (out.any((\ item=mesa_wire/link (eq item.id want.peer.id)))) out
      = ;handle (Spawn (mesa_wire/sender want.host want.port me))
      | out.snoc((mesa_wire/link want.peer.id want.host want.port handle))
  + answer
    ' How a landing went, as the supervisor's answer carries it: 200 when
    ' the event was admitted, else 409 and the reason as a number.
    \ outcome=maybe[pail] now=namespace
    ^ [nat str str]
    ?> (./some refusal) outcome [200 "" ""]
    ?> (./some said) (pail/as[helm/supervisor/rejection] refusal) [409 "0" ""]
    | [409 (nat/show (quip_val said.reason)) ""]
  + why
    \ status=nat body=str
    ^ maybe[iota]
    = none=maybe[iota] .none
      unknown=iota 'net_refused
    ? (eq status 200) none
    ?> (./some n) (nat/parse body) (./some unknown)
    ? (eq 0 n) (./some unknown)
    = reason=iota ($ts n)
    | ./some reason
  + act
    ' Do what the rules ask: hand each peer's packets to its sender as one
    ' batch, and ask the world to admit each landing.
    \ parent=nat links=row[mesa_wire/link] does=row[mesa_foot/effect]
    ^ nat
    = empty=row[nat] []
      ;sent
        | links.fold 0
          \ ;done=nat item=mesa_wire/link
          ^ nat
          = batch
              | does.fold empty
                \ out=row[nat] effect=mesa_foot/effect
                ^ row[nat]
                ?> (./send to packet) effect out
                ? !(eq to item.id) out
                | out.snoc(packet)
          ? !(batch.len) done
          ; (Send item.handle batch)
          done.inc
    | does.fold sent
      \ ;done=nat effect=mesa_foot/effect
      ^ nat
      ?> (./admit request plan) effect done
      ; (Send parent (feet/gift/admit request plan mesa_wire/answer))
      done.inc
  + marked
    ' The rift and the highest announced epoch a mark file holds; zeros
    ' when there is none yet.
    \ file=str
    ^ mesa_wire/mark
    = ;bytes (Try ReadFile file)
    ? bytes
     > (./err _) (mesa_wire/mark 0 0)
     > (./ok held)
      ? (lt (wid held) 17) (mesa_wire/mark 0 0)
      | mesa_wire/mark (loadvar 0 8 held) (loadvar 8 8 held)
  + mark
    : rift=nat top=nat
  + remark
    \ file=str rift=nat top=nat
    ^ nat
    = raw (add (mod rift (bex 64)) (lsh (mod top (bex 64)) 64))
    | WriteFile file (add raw (bex 128))
  + named
    ' A file's path as the foot's record gives it, or where it is kept when
    ' the record says nothing.
    \ said=str kept=str
    ^ str
    ? (eq 0 said.len) kept
    said
  + seed
    ' The world's signing seed, from its ring file. A world that has never
    ' stated a key and has no ring is given one: 32 bytes of the runtime's
    ' entropy, written where the ring is kept, in a folder of the world's
    ' own. A world that has stated a key is never given another: without
    ' its ring it stays silent, because a new seed would be a new identity.
    \ ring=str stated=bool
    ^ nat
    = ;held (Try ReadFile ring)
      found
        ? held
         > (./err _) 0
         > (./ok bytes) bytes
    ? !(eq 0 (mesa_wire/public found)) found
    ? stated 0
    = ;folder (Folder "io/mesa")
      ;fresh (Entropy 32)
      ;wrote (WriteFile ring fresh)
    fresh
  + took
    ' What a file holds, or nothing.
    \ file=str
    ^ nat
    = ;held (Try ReadFile file)
    ? held
     > (./err _) 0
     > (./ok bytes) bytes
  + secret
    ' A secret the foot keeps as a file of its own: read, or made from the
    ' runtime's entropy the first time it is needed, in the folder only
    ' the world can open.
    \ file=str
    ^ nat
    = ;found (mesa_wire/took file)
    ? (gt (wid found) 32) found
    = ;folder (Folder "io/mesa")
      ;fresh (Entropy 32)
      ;wrote (WriteFile file fresh)
    fresh
  + handed
    ' Where a door leaves what it was handed for the foot: a file in
    ' io/mesa/in named by a number and nothing else, so an ask can name no
    ' other file of the world's.
    \ n=nat
    ^ str
    | str/cat "io/mesa/in/" (nat/show n)
  + leave
    ' An invitation's secret, left for this world's door as a file in
    ' io/mesa/out under the invitation's number.
    \ k=desk/keys id=nat
    ^ nat
    ? (eq 0 id) 0
    = ;folder (Folder "io/mesa/out")
      ;wrote (WriteFile (str/cat "io/mesa/out/" (nat/show id)) (desk/invitation k id))
    1
  + desk
    ' Answer the asks the world holds for its foot's desk (desk.foil). The
    ' custody and maker secrets are read only when an ask waits, and are
    ' made the first time. An answered ask that was handed a secret has
    ' its file emptied and is marked spent.
    \ parent=nat links=row[mesa_wire/link] live=nat state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ nat
    = asks (desk/pending foot.self state)
      used (desk/used foot.self state)
    ? (and (eq 0 asks.len) (eq 0 used.len)) 0
    = home (pass/kept (mesa_foot/home foot) state).fall(myth/new)
      ;custody (? (eq 0 asks.len) 0 (mesa_wire/secret (mesa_wire/named home.txt_at(['custody]) "io/mesa/custody")))
      ;maker (? (eq 0 asks.len) 0 (mesa_wire/secret (mesa_wire/named home.txt_at(['maker]) "io/mesa/maker")))
      k (desk/keys live custody maker)
      ;answered
        | asks.fold 0
          \ ;done=nat item=[at=path ask=myth]
          ^ nat
          = [where ask] item
            n ask.nat_at(['handed] 0)
            ;given (? (eq 0 n) 0 (mesa_wire/took (mesa_wire/handed n)))
            ;left (? (equal[str] ask.txt_at(['want]) "link") (mesa_wire/leave k ask.nat_at(['id] 0)) 0)
            turn (desk/answer k given where ask state foot)
          ; (mesa_wire/act parent links turn.does)
          done.inc
    | used.fold answered
      \ ;done=nat item=[at=path handed=nat]
      ^ nat
      = [where n] item
        ;folder (Folder "io/mesa/in")
        ;emptied (WriteFile (mesa_wire/handed n) 1)
        gone=row[[p=path q=writ]] [[where (writ/poke (myth/sing ['spent] (pails/n 1)))]]
      ; (mesa_wire/act parent links (desk/say gone foot).does)
      done.inc
  + run
    ' The foot. It waits for the world as it stands, reads its seed and
    ' its mark, raises its rift when the world is behind what it once
    ' announced, and then runs the rules for whatever arrives.
    ' It listens where its record says: a port that appears on a record
    ' that had none is taken up when it appears, and a foot that is
    ' listening keeps its port until it is stopped.
    \ init=feet/task/init self=nat
    ^ nat
    = record (mesa_wire/own init.ax)
      port record.nat_at(['port] 0)
      ring (mesa_wire/named record.txt_at(['ring]) "io/mesa/ring")
      file (mesa_wire/named record.txt_at(['mark]) "io/mesa/mark")
      claimed (gt record.nat_at(['seq] 0) 0)
      ;seed (mesa_wire/seed ring (claimed || (gt record.nat_at(['key] 0) 0)))
      silent (and claimed !(eq record.nat_at(['key] 0) (mesa_wire/public seed)))
    ? (eq 0 (mesa_wire/public seed))
      ; (Trace ["mesa foot: the ring file holds no seed" ring] 0)
      0
    ; (Send init.parent (feet/gift/state 0))
    = ;world
        % ignored=nat 0
        ^ namespace
        = ;[message caps] (Recv[mesa_wire/task] 0)
        ; (helm/supervisor/close_caps caps)
        ?> (./state request held) message (_ 0)
        held
      ;was (mesa_wire/marked file)
      rift (? (lt world.local.top was.top) was.rift.inc was.rift)
      ;noted (mesa_wire/remark file rift (nmax was.top world.local.top))
      me (mesa_foot/id world.self)
      first (mesa_wire/routes init.ax)
      none=row[mesa_wire/link] []
      no_links=row[mesa_wire/link] []
      no_routes=row[mesa_wire/route] []
      ;links (mesa_wire/wire me first none)
      ;clock (Spawn mesa_wire/ticker)
      ;door (? (eq 0 port) 0 (Listen port))
      helpers (? (eq 0 port) 1 (add 1 mesa_foot/acceptors))
    ; (SendCaps clock 0 [0])
    ; (? (eq 0 port) 0 (mesa_wire/listen door mesa_foot/acceptors))
    ; (? claimed 0 (Send init.parent (feet/gift/pass mesa_wire/here (writ/poke (myth/sing ['key] (pails/n (Ed25519PublicKey seed)))))))
    ; (Trace ["mesa foot listening" port] 0)
    = begun (mesa_foot/start world.self seed rift first.map((\ item=mesa_wire/route item.peer)))
      ;opening (mesa_foot/tick (div (Now 0) 1000000) world begun)
    ; (mesa_wire/act init.parent links opening.does)
    ; (mesa_wire/desk init.parent links seed world opening.foot)
    % foot=mesa_foot/foot opening.foot
      view=namespace world
      reach=row[mesa_wire/link] links
      top=nat (nmax was.top world.local.top)
      beat=nat 0
      left=nat 0
      key=nat seed
      mute=bool silent
      at=nat port
      ear=nat door
    = ;[message caps] (Recv[mesa_wire/task] 0)
      helper
        ? message
         > carried=mesa_wire/heard .true
         > time=mesa_wire/tick .true
        .false
    ; (? (and helper (gt caps.len 0)) (Send caps.at(0) (? left 0 1)) 0)
    ; (helm/supervisor/close_caps caps)
    ? (and helper (eq left 1)) (? (eq 0 ear) 0 (CloseFd ear))
    ? (and helper (gt left 1)) (_ foot view reach top beat left.dec key mute at ear)
    ? (gt left 0) (_ foot view reach top beat left key mute at ear)
    ? (and mute helper) (_ foot view reach top beat left key mute at ear)
    ? message
     > (./committed epoch)
      ; (Send init.parent (feet/gift/state epoch))
      | _ foot view reach top beat left key mute at ear
     > (./state request held)
      = ;turn (mesa_foot/turned held foot)
        ;higher (nmax top held.local.top)
      ; (? (gt higher top) (mesa_wire/remark file foot.rift higher) 0)
      ; (mesa_wire/act init.parent reach turn.does)
      ; (mesa_wire/desk init.parent reach key held turn.foot)
      | _ turn.foot held reach higher beat left key mute at ear
     > (./fact binding)
      = wish (mesa_wire/own binding).nat_at(['port] 0)
        opens (and (eq 0 at) (gt wish 0))
        ;heard (? opens (Listen wish) ear)
        now (? opens wish at)
      ; (? opens (mesa_wire/listen heard mesa_foot/acceptors) 0)
      ; (? opens (Trace ["mesa foot listening" wish] 0) 0)
      ? (mesa_wire/stopped binding)
        ; (mesa_wire/wake now mesa_foot/acceptors)
        ; (mesa_wire/wire me no_routes reach)
        | _ foot view no_links top beat (? (eq 0 now) 1 (add 1 mesa_foot/acceptors)) key mute now heard
      = wanted (mesa_wire/routes binding)
        peers wanted.map((\ item=mesa_wire/route item.peer))
        ;next (mesa_wire/wire me wanted reach)
        own (mesa_wire/own binding)
        stated (gt own.nat_at(['seq] 0) 0)
        want own.nat_at(['key] 0)
        ;fresh (? (and stated !(eq want (mesa_wire/public key))) (ReadFile ring) key)
        agrees (? stated (eq want (mesa_wire/public fresh)) .true)
      ? !agrees (_ foot view next top beat left key .true now heard)
      ? (and (eq fresh key) (and !mute (equal[row[mesa_foot/peer]] peers foot.peers))) (_ foot view next top beat left key mute now heard)
      = ;again (mesa_foot/tick (div (Now 0) 1000000) view (mesa_foot/start view.self fresh foot.rift peers))
      ; (mesa_wire/act init.parent next again.does)
      | _ again.foot view next top beat left fresh .false now heard
     > carried=mesa_wire/heard
      = ;turn
          | carried.packets.fold (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
            \ ;acc=mesa_foot/turn packet=nat
            ^ mesa_foot/turn
            | mesa_foot/after acc
              \ now=mesa_foot/foot
              ^ mesa_foot/turn
              | mesa_foot/heard carried.from packet view now
      ; (mesa_wire/act init.parent reach turn.does)
      | _ turn.foot view reach top beat left key mute at ear
     > time=mesa_wire/tick
      = again (eq 0 (mod beat.inc mesa_foot/every))
        ;turn (? again (mesa_foot/tick time.now view foot) (mesa_foot/clock time.now view foot))
      ; (mesa_wire/act init.parent reach turn.does)
      | _ turn.foot view reach top beat.inc left key mute at ear
     > (./admitted request status body line)
      = ;turn (mesa_foot/landed request (mesa_wire/why status body) foot)
      ; (mesa_wire/act init.parent reach turn.does)
      | _ turn.foot view reach top beat left key mute at ear
     > (./ack err) (_ foot view reach top beat left key mute at ear)
    | _ foot view reach top beat left key mute at ear
  + here
    ^ path
    []
  + public
    ' The public key of a seed; 0 when the bytes are not a seed.
    \ seed=nat
    ^ nat
    ? !(eq 33 (wid seed)) 0
    | Ed25519PublicKey seed
  + stopped
    ' Whether the foot's record says to stop: it is gone, or holds `stop`.
    \ binding=axal[saga]
    ^ bool
    ?> (./some version) binding.fil .true
    | gt (unpin version.myth).nat_at(['stop] 0) 0
  + wake
    ' Connect to this world's own port, once for each acceptor, so that
    ' each stops waiting and asks the foot whether to go on.
    \ port=nat count=nat
    ^ nat
    = nothing=row[nat] []
    % left=nat count
    ^ nat
    ? (eq 0 port) 0
    ? !(left) 0
    ; (SendTo 0 "127.0.0.1" port (mesa_wire/frames 0 nothing))
    | _ left.dec
  + listen
    ' Start the acceptors that share the listening socket.
    \ fd=nat count=nat
    ^ nat
    % left=nat count
    ^ nat
    ? !(left) 0
    = ;one (Spawn (mesa_wire/acceptor fd))
    ; (SendCaps one 0 [0])
    | _ left.dec
